WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.800
The engine compartment fire is the most dangerous one on a small boat, and your instinct will be wrong.

2
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:10.200
Your instinct says: open the hatch and look.

3
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:11.850
Don’t.

4
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.775
Here’s the drill.

5
00:00:14.025 --> 00:00:19.275
Shut down the engines, the generator and the blowers, and close the fuel valves.

6
00:00:19.525 --> 00:00:23.175
Close the vents and hatches to starve the fire of air.

7
00:00:23.425 --> 00:00:25.375
And leave the hatch shut.

8
00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.750
What happens if you open it?

9
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.625
A rush of fresh air, and the fire flares up in your face.

10
00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:37.050
Discharge the fixed system, if it hasn’t gone off by itself.

11
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.050
Many systems shut the engines down when they fire.

12
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.850
Then wait.

13
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:49.500
At least fifteen minutes before you open that compartment, so it can cool and the fire can’t reignite.

14
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:53.975
And when you do open it, have a portable extinguisher in your hand.
